cks featuring extremely formidable  women from 1990s nikita to 1997's the  fifth element to 2014's lucy for his  latest exploration of this theme he  recruited russian supermodel sasha luss  for the title role in anna the story of  an everyday woman who happens to look  like a russian supermodel and somehow  becomes a cold-blooded killer for the  kgb if it all sounds a little familiar  critics agreed many found the film so  highly reminiscent of besson's previous  work that it bordered on self parody  this may have been fine if the picture  were serviceably made but most observers  found bason to be stuck firmly in  neutral with anna a sparsely plotted  film with a distinct lack of imagination  the guardian's benjamin lee said that  what ultimately sings the film is its  overwhelming blandness from the lack of  creativity employed in anna's many kills  to bassan's inability to choreograph a  pulse racing action scene and the  scripts be labored attempts to jump back  and forward in time to wrongfooters only  highlight how little it brings to the  table meanwhile peter sabzinski of  rogereber.com critiqued the film for not  living up to bassan's previous works  even long-standing fans of his will find  it hard to muster much enthusiasm for  the startlingly lazy bit of by the  numbers hack work in short most critics  responses were best summed up in one  line i  am very disappointed  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

